11. Network Diagnostics — Tcpdump, Netcat & OpenSSL

Tcpdump

Capture authorized lab traffic:

sudo tcpdump -i any -nn -c 100 -w lab.pcap

Netcat

Test whether a lab service is reachable:

nc -vz <LAB_IP> 22
nc -vz <LAB_IP> 443

OpenSSL

Inspect a TLS connection and certificate chain:

openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 \
  -servername example.com </dev/null

Curl

Inspect HTTP response headers:

curl -sS -D - -o /dev/null https://example.com

These tools help investigate connectivity, service exposure, TLS configuration, and protocol behavior.

